Description: Longitudinal study examining heterogeneity in self-control
    development from ages 3-17 using Millennium Cohort Study data. Employs
    confirmatory factor analysis, measurement invariance testing, latent
    growth models, structural equation model trees, and growth mixture
    models to identify developmental subgroups and their predictors.
